{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "3a7d9e1c-4b2f-4a6e-8c9d-1f2e3a4b5c6d",
		"name": "Petclinic - API Exploration",
		"description": "Manual exploration collection covering every endpoint defined in src/main/resources/openapi.yml, organized by resource. Unlike petclinic-nonregressiontests.postman_collection.json (the scripted CI/Newman regression suite), this collection is meant for ad-hoc, interactive use against a locally running instance (`mvn spring-boot:run`, default port 9966, context path /petclinic).\n\nUsage:\n1. Select the 'Petclinic Exploration Env' environment.\n2. Run requests top-to-bottom within a folder: 'Create' requests capture the returned id into an environment variable (ownerId, petId, visitId, petTypeId, vetId, specialtyId) which subsequent requests in that folder reuse.\n3. If petclinic.security.enable=true, add Basic Auth credentials at the collection or request level.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Owners",
